      "settings": {
        "custom_liquid": "<div style=\"padding-right: 40px; padding-left: 40px; max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto;\">\n<div class=\"bg-section\">\n\n  <h2>Sell Your Products. Fund Real Causes. <br>Do Nothing Different.</h2>\n\n  <p>Here's the pitch: we sell your products on our marketplace. You earn your normal wholesale margin. A real chunk of every sale goes directly to a nonprofit. The charitable donation comes from our side, not yours.</p>\n\n  <p>You sacrifice nothing. You change nothing. You gain a new sales channel and a genuine impact story you didn't have to pay for.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>We'll pause here so you can re-read that, because most people think there's a catch. There isn't.</strong></p>\n\n  <hr>\n\n  <h2>How It Works for Brands</h2>\n  <h3>The Whole Thing Takes 5 Minutes</h3>\n\n  <p><strong>Step 1: We connect on Shopify Collective.</strong><br>\n  Shopify's built-in tool for store-to-store selling. You're probably already on Shopify. This is a native feature. No apps. No contracts. No fees. Just a connection request that you accept.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Step 2: You set your wholesale price.</strong><br>\n  Same price you'd give any other retail partner. We don't ask for special pricing. Unless it makes sense for the charity we're giving to. Then we'll talk.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Step 3: We list your products at your retail price.</strong><br>\n  We never undercut you. We never discount your products below what you sell them for on your own site. Your brand, your pricing, our platform.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Step 4: Someone buys your product on our site.</strong><br>\n  The order routes directly to you through Shopify. You fulfill it the same way you fulfill any other order. Same warehouse. Same shipping. Same everything. You've done this a million times.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Step 5: You get paid your wholesale cost. We handle the rest.</strong><br>\n  The difference between retail and your wholesale cost is our margin — and we send a big portion of that to a nonprofit partner (always more than we get, guaranteed). That's our business model. You just got paid normally.</p>\n\n  <p>That's it. No inventory risk. No upfront cost. No commitment. No contract. If it's not working, either of us can disconnect anytime. But it will work, because we're essentially handing you free orders.</p>\n\n  <hr>\n\n  <h2>The Money Part</h2>\n  <h3>Let's Talk About What Everyone's Actually Thinking</h3>\n\n  <p><strong>\"If you're giving so much to charity, what's in it for my brand?\"</strong><br>\n  Your normal wholesale margin on every single order. Nothing changes for you financially. Zero. You earn the same amount per unit as you would selling through any other retailer. We don't ask you to discount. We don't ask you to donate. We don't take a commission. Your wholesale price is your wholesale price.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>\"Where does the charitable donation come from?\"</strong><br>\n  From us. The difference between your wholesale cost and the retail price — that's our gross margin. We take a thin operating cut and send the rest to charity. Yes, this means our margins are very thin. Yes, our accountant has expressed concerns. No, we're not changing the model.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>\"Do I get to choose which charity?\"</strong><br>\n  Yes. When you join, we match your products with a nonprofit partner based on your category — outdoor brands might fund ocean conservation, beauty brands might fund women's empowerment. But if you have a cause you care about, tell us. We'll make the match. You can change it anytime. Some of our best campaigns are brand-specific partnerships — like Johnnie-O x ALS Network, where every Johnnie-O product sold on our site funds ALS research.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>\"What if I don't want to be associated with a specific cause?\"</strong><br>\n  Totally fine. We have general nonprofit partners that cover broad impact areas. No brand is forced into a cause that doesn't feel right. This is supposed to be good for everyone, not awkward.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>\"Will you undercut my pricing?\"</strong><br>\n  Never. We sell at your retail price. Period. Your DTC site, your Amazon listings, your other retail partners — we never go below any of them. Your brand integrity is non-negotiable for us because if we undercut you, you'd leave, and then we'd have no products, and then we'd have no charity to fund, and then what was even the point.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>\"Is there a minimum commitment?\"</strong><br>\n  No. No minimums. No contracts. No lock-in. Connect through Shopify Collective, let us import some products, and see what happens. If you get orders, great. If you don't like it, disconnect. We're confident enough in the model to let the results speak for themselves.</p>\n\n  <hr>\n\n  <h2>What You Get</h2>\n  <h3>The Benefits, Without the Corporate Jargon</h3>\n\n  <p><strong>A new sales channel that costs you nothing to set up.</strong><br>\n  5 minutes on Shopify Collective. That's the total investment of your time. We've seen founders do it while waiting for their coffee.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Orders you wouldn't have gotten otherwise.</strong><br>\n  Our customers are shopping specifically because their purchase funds a cause. These aren't people who were going to buy from your site and got redirected. These are incremental sales from an audience that's motivated by impact. They found us because they wanted to shop with purpose. You benefit because you make great products.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>A real CSR story you didn't have to manufacture.</strong><br>\n  \"Our products fund [Nonprofit Name] through Boundless Giving\" is a better press line than \"We donated 1% of Q4 profits to a foundation we started ourselves.\" Use it on your site. Put it in your emails. Post about it. We'll send you the exact dollar amounts so you can share the impact. Free content, basically.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Your brand shown to a cause-conscious audience.</strong><br>\n  Our shoppers care about where their money goes, they're skeptical of greenwashing, and they have disposable income. They're the audience every DTC brand is trying to reach. Except on our platform, they're actively looking to buy from brands with an impact story. You already have one — you just didn't know it yet.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Zero risk.</strong><br>\n  No inventory commitment. No upfront payment. No minimum orders. No exclusivity. You continue selling everywhere else you already sell. We're just another channel — except this one comes with a built-in charitable impact story and customers who are specifically looking for brands they can feel good about supporting.</p>\n\n  <hr>\n\n  <h2>Select Brands Already on Boundless Giving</h2>\n\n  <p>Johnnie-O · Faherty · Outerknown · L*Space · Cleobella · Vitamin A · White + Warren · Nili Lotan · Paige · Saint Croix · Le Mer · Amber Interiors · Le Bon Shoppe · Sammy + Nat ·  Quiksilver · Surfside Supply and more joining every week.</p>\n\n  <p>If these brands trust us, you probably can too. Or don't trust us and just try it anyway — it's free and takes 5 minutes. Worst case you wasted the same amount of time you'd spend deciding what to have for lunch.</p>\n\n  <hr>\n\n  <h2>Ready? It's Actually Easy.</h2>\n\n  <p><strong>Option 1: Shopify Collective.</strong><br>\n  If you're on Shopify, search for \"Boundless Giving\" in the Collective supplier directory and send us a connection request. Or we'll send you one. Either way, 5 minutes.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Option 2: Email us.</strong><br>\n  <a href=\"mailto:info@boundlessgiving.com\">info@boundlessgiving.com</a> — tell us your brand name and your Shopify URL. We'll handle the rest.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Option 3: Just reply to whatever email got you here.</strong><br>\n  We read everything. We respond fast. We're a small team that cares too much. It's kind of our thing.</p>\n\n</div>",
